Subject: [PATCH] nuttx: reserve synchronization storage for embedded PI holders

NuttX 13.1 with CONFIG_PRIORITY_INHERITANCE=y and
CONFIG_SEM_PREALLOCHOLDERS=0 embeds one holder record in each semaphore.
On the selected 32-bit targets this adds three words per native semaphore
compared with the positive global-pool configuration. A pthread rwlock
contains both a mutex and a condition variable, so it needs six more words.

Keep these bindings opaque and preserve their existing spare capacity.
Native init/destroy functions still own their representation. Larger storage
does not qualify the all-zero libc initializers as native initializers.
The build's target-header ABI gate must check actual size and alignment for
the selected configuration before accepting a firmware build.

diff --git a/src/unix/nuttx/mod.rs b/src/unix/nuttx/mod.rs
--- a/src/unix/nuttx/mod.rs
+++ b/src/unix/nuttx/mod.rs
@@ -268,10 +268,10 @@
 const __SOCKADDR_STORAGE_SIZE__: usize = 36;
 const __PTHREAD_ATTR_SIZE__: usize = 5;
-const __PTHREAD_MUTEX_SIZE__: usize = 9;
-const __PTHREAD_COND_SIZE__: usize = 7;
+const __PTHREAD_MUTEX_SIZE__: usize = 12;
+const __PTHREAD_COND_SIZE__: usize = 10;
 const __PTHREAD_CONDATTR_SIZE__: usize = 5;
-const __PTHREAD_RWLOCK_SIZE__: usize = 17;
-const __SEM_SIZE__: usize = 6;
+const __PTHREAD_RWLOCK_SIZE__: usize = 23;
+const __SEM_SIZE__: usize = 9;
 const __NAME_MAX__: usize = 64;
 const __FDSET_SIZE__: usize = 10;
 const __SIGSET_SIZE__: usize = 8;
